{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Then they will acknowledge that to the Name alone belongs the kingship. And the verse is like <b>and the prophecy of Oded the prophet</b>, whose meaning is <b>the prophecy, the prophecy of Oded</b>, and many are like it. It is as though it said: For to YHWH belongs the kingship, and YHWH rules over the nations."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Resolved HaShem as YHWH in the paraphrase of Psalms 22:29, consistent with the divine-name rule for biblical citation; the first occurrence לשם refers to the divine Name and is rendered 'to the Name.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:19.969803589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}